 a method for using haplotype trees in phenotype/genotype association studies</article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>2005</year><volume>169</volume><fpage>441</fpage><lpage>453</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15371364</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1534/genetics.104.030080</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tzeng</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evolutionary-based grouping of haplotypes in association analysis</article-title><source>Genet Epidemiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>220</fpage><lpage>231</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15726584</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/gepi.20063</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lyngs&#x000f8;</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Song</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hein</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Minimum recombination histories by branch and bound, proceedings of workshop on algorithms in bioinformatics</article-title><source>Lect Notes Comput Sci</source><year>2005</year><volume>3692</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>250</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Felsenstein</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source>PHYLIP (Phylogeny Inference Package) Version 36</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Seattle: Department of Genome Sciences, University of Washington</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scheet</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Stephens</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A fast and f